// Hand-written weakening ideal.
//
// The specification is unrealizable because the biconditional forces the
// system to decide `F G !p` — a property of the whole infinite future of an
// input — at every point at which it chooses `acc`. Emitting `acc` forever
// loses whenever the environment holds `p` high forever; withholding it
// forever loses whenever the environment drops `p` forever.
//
// AuRUS's own repairs for this example (case-studies/syntcomp-unreal/
// ltl2dba27/genuine/ltl2dba{22,24}.tlsf) replace `F G !p` with `G p` and
// `F p` respectively, which are unrelated properties rather than weakenings:
// take p always true and acc always false, and the original biconditional
// holds while ltl2dba22's does not. They are other Acacia+ benchmark
// instances, not repairs of this one.
//
// Dropping the right-to-left direction keeps the liveness intent — an
// eventually-quiet input is still acknowledged infinitely often — and
// discards only the obligation to withhold `acc` on the strength of an
// unobservable future.
INFO {
  TITLE:       "LTL -> DBA  -  Example 27"
  DESCRIPTION: "One of the Acacia+ example files"
  SEMANTICS:   Mealy
  TARGET:      Mealy
}

MAIN {

  INPUTS {
    p;
  }

  OUTPUTS {
    acc;
  }

  GUARANTEES {
    F G !p -> G F acc;
  }

}
